<title>USA: 3Com, U.S. Robotics up in late trading.</title>
<headline>3Com, U.S. Robotics up in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Robotics shares were up more than 10 points, to 71-1/2, and 3Com Corp was up 2 points to 41 in late trading on Wednesday before Nasdaq halted both stocks after news of their proposed merger broke.</p>
<p>U.S. Robotics had closed at 61 on Nasdaq, down 1/2 of a point, during regular trading. Its 52-week high was 105-1/2.</p>
<p>3Com had closed at 39 on Nasdaq, down 1/8 during regular trading. Its 52-week high was 81-3/8.</p>
<p>After the market closed, 3Com announced it would buy modem giant U.S. Robotics in a $6.6 billion deal.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
